 clr"><article id="post-12027"><ul class="meta ospm-default clr"><li class="meta-cat"><span class="screen-reader-text">Post category:</span><i class=" icon-folder" aria-hidden="true" role="img"></i><a href="https://www.ptebank.com/category/exam-tips/" rel="category tag">Exam Tips</a></li><li class="meta-rt"><span class="screen-reader-text">Reading time:</span><i class=" icon-cup" aria-hidden="true" role="img"></i>4 mins read</li></ul><div class="entry-content clr" itemprop="text"><h1 class="wp-block-heading">Latest PTE real exam questions</h1><p>Are you going to take PTE test soon? Please check following PTE new question updates. And if you want a full version of it, go to <a href="https://www.ptebank.com/product/pteprediction/"><strong><span style="color: #3366ff;"><em>PTE Prediction File for January 2025.</em></span></strong></a> We are constantly collecting new questions to ensure you are always equipped with up-to-dated questions and model answers. Practicing these questions would not only benefit you in exam preparation but also help you to anticipate what will be tested. </p><div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="1024" height="791" src="https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Promotion-1-1-1024x791.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-12031" srcset="https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Promotion-1-1-1024x791.jpg 1024w, https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Promotion-1-1-scaled-600x464.jpg 600w, https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Promotion-1-1-768x593.jpg 768w, https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Promotion-1-1-1536x1187.jpg 1536w, https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Promotion-1-1-2048x1583.jpg 2048w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure></div><h1 class="wp-block-heading">PTE New Questions January &#8211; <strong>Read Aloud:</strong></h1><p><b>Bill</b></p><p class="p2">The bill calls for the establishment of the National Landslide Hazards Reduction Program within one year of becoming law. The program serves numerous functions, including to identify and understand landslide hazards and risks, reduce losses from landslides, protect communities at risk of landslides hazards, and improve communication and emergency preparedness.</p><p><b>Agricultural Problems</b></p><p class="p2">Agricultural problems due to climate change of normal weather, water depletion and the collapse of soil have become big problems in all parts of the world. Many are now focusing on ethics and family farming as a way to combat these issues.</p><p><b>Innovation Product</b></p><p class="p2">An innovative new product or service can give a firm a head start over its rivals, which can be difficult for a new entrant to overcome. If the new technology is also patented, then other firms cannot simply copy its design. It is legally protected.</p><p><b>Urban Forests</b></p><p class="p2">A community&#8217;s urban forest is an extension of its pride and community spirit. Trees enhance community economic stability by attracting businesses and tourists as people tend to linger and shop longer along tree-lined streets. Apartments and offices in wooded areas rent more quickly and businesses leasing office spaces in developments with trees reported higher productivity and fewer absences.</p><p><b>Root Network</b></p><p class="p2">The networks of roots that plants use to absorb water and nutrients can encompass a space larger than the part of the plant visible above ground. The nature of these roots systems can help plants adapt to challenging environments such as deserts. For instance, mesquite trees can develop tap roots capable of digging more than 50 yards deep to reach water.</p><h1 class="wp-block-heading">PTE New Questions January &#8211; <strong>Describe Image:</strong></h1><h2 class="wp-block-heading">Food Pyramid &#8211; PTE Describe Image</h2><p><noscript><img decoding="async" class="alignnone wp-image-12028 size-full" src="https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Food-Pyramid.jpg" alt="" width="612" height="461" srcset="https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Food-Pyramid.jpg 612w, https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Food-Pyramid-600x452.jpg 600w" sizes="(max-width: 612px) 100vw, 612px" /></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%20612%20461%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' decoding="async" class="lazyload alignnone wp-image-12028 size-full" data-src="https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Food-Pyramid.jpg" alt="" width="612" height="461" data-srcset="https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Food-Pyramid.jpg 612w, https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Food-Pyramid-600x452.jpg 600w" data-sizes="(max-width: 612px) 100vw, 612px" /></p><h2><strong>Plastic Recycling &#8211; PTE Describe Image</strong></h2><p><noscript><img decoding="async" class="alignnone wp-image-12029 size-full" src="https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/plastic_recycling.png" alt="" width="1600" height="1690" srcset="https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/plastic_recycling.png 1600w, https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/plastic_recycling-600x634.png 600w, https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/plastic_recycling-969x1024.png 969w, https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/plastic_recycling-768x811.png 768w, https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/plastic_recycling-1454x1536.png 1454w" sizes="(max-width: 1600px) 100vw, 1600px" /></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%201600%201690%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' decoding="async" class="lazyload alignnone wp-image-12029 size-full" data-src="https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/plastic_recycling.png" alt="" width="1600" height="1690" data-srcset="https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/plastic_recycling.png 1600w, https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/plastic_recycling-600x634.png 600w, https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/plastic_recycling-969x1024.png 969w, https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/plastic_recycling-768x811.png 768w, https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/plastic_recycling-1454x1536.png 1454w" data-sizes="(max-width: 1600px) 100vw, 1600px" /></p><h2><strong>Chocolate Consumers &#8211; PTE Describe Image</strong></h2><figure id="attachment_9551" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-9551" style="width: 906px" class="wp-caption alignnone"><noscript><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="wp-image-9551 size-full" src="https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/chocolate_consumers.png" alt="Chocolate Consumers PTE DI" width="906" height="568" srcset="https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/chocolate_consumers.png 906w, https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/chocolate_consumers-600x376.png 600w, https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/chocolate_consumers-768x481.png 768w" sizes="(max-width: 906px) 100vw, 906px" /></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%20906%20568%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="lazyload wp-image-9551 size-full" data-src="https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/chocolate_consumers.png" alt="Chocolate Consumers PTE DI" width="906" height="568" data-srcset="https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/chocolate_consumers.png 906w, https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/chocolate_consumers-600x376.png 600w, https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/chocolate_consumers-768x481.png 768w" data-sizes="(max-width: 906px) 100vw, 906px" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-9551" class="wp-caption-text">Chocolate Consumers PTE DI</figcaption></figure><h1> </h1><h1>PTE New Questions January &#8211; Retell Lecture &#8211; Truth and Rhetoric</h1> <audio class="wp-audio-shortcode" id="audio-12027-1" preload="none" style="width: 100%;" controls="controls"><source type="audio/mpeg" src="https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/Truth-and-Rhetoric.mp3?_=1" /><a href="https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/Truth-and-Rhetoric.mp3">https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/Truth-and-Rhetoric.mp3</a></audio><p class="p1">But Aristotle says the reason we need rhetoric is we have to be able to use it. We have to be able to use rhetoric influence, basically, the rebel, and the morons. We try to get them to understand truth. Truth is suggested, is different than rhetoric. Rhetoric is the dressing, is the body, right? Truth is the spirit, is the soul, is abstract. It doesn’t have a body. It’s not particular. If you wanna get somebody to the truth, you might have to use some kind of tricks. Right? Because most people are not sound and can&#8217;t see the truth. That’s what we think. Most people are ramble. Really. Only the educated be erudite are actually capable of seeing the truth. If you wanna get the general mass there, you may have to do fable a little bit. So Aristotle that is rhetoric. Rhetoric is something that is used to influence people. Right? And it’s a kind of mentally promised a logic.</p><p class="p4"><b>Sample Answer:</b></p><p class="p1">Aristotle in his work Rhetoric reveals how truth is related to rhetoric. He believes that truth and rhetoric is different. Rhetoric is the body, while truth is the spirit, the soul. Though some people are rational, they do not understand truth. Therefore, in his view, we should use rhetoric to help people to understand truth. If you want to make people get into truth, you have to use tricks because truth itself is abstract.</p><h1>PTE New Questions January &#8211; Summarize Spoken Text:</h1><ul><li><span style="color: #3366ff;"><a style="color: #3366ff;" href="https://www.ptebank.com/product/ptepred